<!-- @after 12. Further Reading :: recap -->
### Say these in the interview

- Keep evaluation pure; log exposure only where the rendered experience first differs, including the control arm.
- Loading is not non-enrollment. Wait for a consistent identity snapshot before showing experiment-sensitive UI.
- Use server assignments, eligibility and holdout decisions; an unknown assignment is not a treatment bucket.
- Freeze experiment definitions or use versioned sticky assignments; modulo a changing variant list reshuffles users.
- A live kill overrides a pin, and analysis joins later outcomes to the first valid exposure. Check sample ratio mismatch rather than trusting event counts.
